            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "U.S. Treasury Yields Move Higher, Fed Rate Cut Looms Next Week",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "U.S. Treasury yields were rising in Asian trade, even as August CPI data published Thursday are unlikely to be a game changer in the Federal Reserve's policy outlook.  Following the data, \"we left both our Fed outlook and our inflation forecasts unchanged,\" Pimco's Tiffany Wilding said in a note.  Accordingly, Pimco expects a 25-basis-point rate cut next week, \"though 50 [basis points] will likely be discussed,\" the economist said.",
