        {
          "id": "1e365f12-d3cb-3eac-8904-73c60b3cb261",
          "content": {
            "id": "1e365f12-d3cb-3eac-8904-73c60b3cb261",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Ten-Year Treasury Yield Dips Below 4%",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "A jump in weekly jobless claims and largely as-expected inflation data boosted bonds on Thursday, briefly driving the yield on the 10-year Treasury note below 4% for the first time since April.  Although overall consumer prices rose a little more than expected last month, the increase in core prices matched economists' forecasts on both a monthly and annual basis.  Meanwhile, weekly jobless claims rose to 263,000, ahead of expectations.",
