            "title": "U.S. 10-Year Treasury Yield Expected to Move Toward 4%",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "The 10-year U.S. Treasury yield is anticipated to test 4% and likely break below it, ING rates strategists Benjamin Schroeder and Padhraic Garvey said in a note.  The strategists maintain the view that the neutral level for the 10-year Treasury yield is in the 4.24%-4.50% area.  The 10-year U.S. Treasury yield was up 2.5 basis points at 4.056%, according to Tradeweb.",
