            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "U.S. Treasury Yields Edge Higher",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "\"The U.S. labor market looks set to remain in focus today, as the BLS' preliminary benchmark revisions to the establishment survey stand as the main event of the upcoming session,\" said Pepperstone's Michael Brown in a note.  Other drivers for the U.S. Treasury market to watch include a $58 billion auction of three-year notes.  The two-year Treasury yield rose 0.8 bp to 3.502%; the 10-year Treasury yield rose 0.7 bp to 4.051%, while the 30-year yield was up 0.9 bp at 4.698%, according to Tradeweb.",
